---
import MainLayout from "../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
import Navbar from "../components/Navbar.astro";
import { siteContent } from "../data/site";
import "../styles/legal.css";

const { companyName, logo, nav, cta, contactInfo } = siteContent;
const phoneHref = `tel:${contactInfo.phone.replace(/[^0-9+]/g, "")}`;
---

<MainLayout
  title="Website Terms of Use | Velixon"
  description="Review the terms that govern access to velixon.net, including acceptable use, intellectual property, third-party links, and important limitations."
>
  <Navbar companyName={companyName} logo={logo} nav={nav} cta={cta} currentPath="/terms" />
  <main id="main-content" class="legal-page">
    <header class="legal-hero">
      <div class="container legal-hero-inner">
        <p class="legal-eyebrow">Trust center · Terms</p>
        <h1>Clear terms for using this website.</h1>
        <p class="legal-lede">These Terms of Use set the ground rules for accessing velixon.net. Client projects and paid services are governed by their own written agreements.</p>
        <p class="legal-meta">
          <span><strong>Effective:</strong> <time datetime="2026-07-15">July 15, 2026</time></span>
          <span><strong>Applies to:</strong> velixon.net</span>
        </p>

        <div class="legal-summary" aria-label="Terms of use summary">
          <div class="legal-summary-item"><span class="legal-summary-number">01 · USE FAIRLY</span><p>Use the site lawfully and do not interfere with its operation or security.</p></div>
          <div class="legal-summary-item"><span class="legal-summary-number">02 · OWNERSHIP MATTERS</span><p>Velixon content remains ours unless a written agreement says otherwise.</p></div>
          <div class="legal-summary-item"><span class="legal-summary-number">03 · PROJECTS ARE SEPARATE</span><p>An inquiry does not create a client relationship or project commitment.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="container legal-content legal-layout">
      <nav class="legal-toc" aria-label="Terms of use contents">
        <p class="legal-toc-title">On this page</p>
        <ol>
          <li><a href="#acceptance">Acceptance</a></li>
          <li><a href="#website">Website purpose</a></li>
          <li><a href="#acceptable-use">Acceptable use</a></li>
          <li><a href="#content">Intellectual property</a></li>
          <li><a href="#submissions">Information you submit</a></li>
          <li><a href="#third-parties">Third parties</a></li>
          <li><a href="#disclaimers">Disclaimers</a></li>
          <li><a href="#liability">Liability</a></li>
          <li><a href="#changes">Changes and contact</a></li>
        </ol>
      </nav>

      <article class="legal-article" aria-label="Velixon Website Terms of Use">
        <section class="legal-section" id="acceptance">
          <p class="legal-section-label">01 · Agreement</p>
          <h2>Acceptance of these terms</h2>
          <p>By accessing or using velixon.net, you agree to these Terms of Use and the <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>. If you do not agree, do not use the website.</p>
          <p>You must be legally able to enter into these terms. If you use the website for a company or other organization, you represent that you have authority to act for that organization.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section" id="website">
          <p class="legal-section-label">02 · Purpose</p>
          <h2>What the website provides</h2>
          <p>This website describes Velixon, our capabilities, products, process, and potential engagements. Its content is general information, not professional legal, financial, tax, compliance, or security advice.</p>
          <p>Submitting a contact form, scheduling a conversation, or exchanging preliminary information does not create a client, partnership, fiduciary, employment, or other professional relationship. A project begins only when the parties sign an applicable written agreement.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section" id="acceptable-use">
          <p class="legal-section-label">03 · Conduct</p>
          <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
          <p>You may use the website for lawful informational and business purposes. You may not:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Break the law, infringe another person's rights, or misrepresent your identity or affiliation.</li>
            <li>Attempt to bypass access controls, probe for vulnerabilities without authorization, or interfere with website availability.</li>
            <li>Introduce malware, harmful code, automated spam, or abusive traffic.</li>
            <li>Scrape, copy, republish, or commercially exploit substantial site content except as permitted by law or written approval.</li>
            <li>Use the site to transmit confidential, unlawful, deceptive, or harmful material.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Velixon may restrict access or take reasonable protective action when we believe use threatens the website, another person, or our rights.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section" id="content">
          <p class="legal-section-label">04 · Ownership</p>
          <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
          <p>Unless stated otherwise, the website and its text, designs, graphics, branding, software, and other content are owned by Velixon or used with permission and are protected by applicable intellectual-property laws.</p>
          <p>Velixon grants you a limited, revocable, nonexclusive, nontransferable right to view and use the website for its intended purpose. No ownership or broader license is transferred. Product names, logos, and marks may not be used in a way that suggests endorsement or affiliation without permission.</p>
          <p>Ownership of client deliverables, preexisting materials, open-source components, and licensed assets is determined by the applicable project agreement—not these website terms.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section" id="submissions">
          <p class="legal-section-label">05 · Submissions</p>
          <h2>Information you submit</h2>
          <p>You remain responsible for information and materials you send. You represent that you have the right to provide them and that doing so does not violate another person's rights or an obligation of confidentiality.</p>
          <p>You give Velixon permission to use submissions only as reasonably necessary to review the inquiry, respond, prevent misuse, maintain business records, and provide services if the parties later agree.</p>
          <div class="legal-callout">
            <strong>An initial inquiry is not a confidential engagement.</strong>
            <p>Do not send trade secrets, credentials, regulated data, source code, or other sensitive material before we have agreed on an appropriate secure channel and any necessary written terms.</p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section" id="third-parties">
          <p class="legal-section-label">06 · External services</p>
          <h2>Third-party links and services</h2>
          <p>The website may link to or rely on third-party websites, platforms, tools, and content. Those third parties control their own services, terms, privacy practices, availability, and security. A link does not necessarily mean Velixon endorses or guarantees the third party.</p>
          <p>You are responsible for reviewing third-party terms before using their services. Velixon is not responsible for third-party content or conduct to the extent permitted by law.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section" id="disclaimers">
          <p class="legal-section-label">07 · Disclaimers</p>
          <h2>Website provided as available</h2>
          <p>Velixon works to keep the website useful, accurate, and available, but content may be incomplete, outdated, or interrupted. To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, the website is provided “as is” and “as available,” without warranties of uninterrupted operation, error-free content, fitness for a particular purpose, noninfringement, or results.</p>
          <p>Nothing on the website promises a specific business, financial, technical, search-ranking, or operational outcome. Project commitments and warranties, if any, appear only in the applicable signed agreement.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section" id="liability">
          <p class="legal-section-label">08 · Limits</p>
          <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
          <p>To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, Velixon and its owners, team members, contractors, and service providers will not be liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, exemplary, or punitive damages, or for lost profits, revenue, data, goodwill, or business opportunity arising from use of—or inability to use—the website.</p>
          <p>Where liability cannot be excluded, Velixon's total liability arising from the website will not exceed the greater of the amount you paid Velixon specifically for website access during the prior twelve months or one hundred U.S. dollars. Some jurisdictions do not allow certain exclusions or limits, so portions of this section may not apply to you.</p>
          <p>These limitations apply only to use of this public website. A signed client agreement may provide different rights and responsibilities.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section" id="changes">
          <p class="legal-section-label">09 · General</p>
          <h2>Changes, enforceability, and contact</h2>
          <p>We may update these terms as the website or our practices change. The effective date above identifies the current version. Continued use after an update means you accept the revised terms to the extent permitted by law.</p>
          <p>If any provision is found unenforceable, the remaining provisions remain in effect. Failure to enforce a provision is not a waiver. Applicable mandatory consumer protections are not limited by these terms.</p>
          <p>Questions about these terms can be sent using the contact details below.</p>
        </section>

        <aside class="legal-contact" aria-labelledby="terms-contact-title">
          <h2 id="terms-contact-title">Questions about these terms?</h2>
          <p>Contact Velixon for a plain-language answer. Project-specific terms are addressed in the written agreement for that engagement.</p>
          <div class="legal-contact-links">
            <a href={`mailto:${contactInfo.email}?subject=Website%20Terms%20Question`}>{contactInfo.email}</a>
            <a href={phoneHref}>{contactInfo.phone}</a>
            <a href="/contact/">Contact form</a>
          </div>
          <div class="legal-related"><strong>Related:</strong> <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a><a href="/security/">Security</a></div>
        </aside>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
</MainLayout>
